---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro'
import Nav from '../components/sections/Nav.astro'
import Footer from '../components/sections/Footer.astro'
import Closing from '../components/marketing/Closing.astro'
import WorkspaceImage from '../components/marketing/WorkspaceImage.astro'
import MeshGarden from '../components/marketing/MeshGarden.astro'
import Substrate from '../components/marketing/Substrate.astro'
import BlogArt from '../components/blog/BlogArt.astro'
const essays = [
  {
    slug: 'the-hundred-year-machine',
    title: 'Software you can keep.',
    label: 'The Hundred-Year Machine',
    text: 'If its maker vanished tonight, what would still work in the morning?'
  },
  {
    slug: 'data-should-work-like-soil',
    title: 'Give your ideas common ground.',
    label: 'Data Should Work Like Soil',
    text: 'A living network grows from the things people bring to it.'
  },
  {
    slug: 'the-workshop-and-the-walled-garden',
    title: 'Leave the workshop open.',
    label: 'The Workshop and the Walled Garden',
    text: 'The tools should be yours to understand, adapt, and build upon.'
  }
]
---

<Base
  title="xNet — A workspace of your own"
  description="An open, local-first workspace for notes, projects, and saved knowledge. Explore the alpha today, and the vision for software and communities you can truly own."
>
  <Nav />
  <main id="main-content">
    <section class="home-hero m-wrap">
      <div>
        <p class="m-eyebrow">A workspace of your own · Open alpha</p>
        <h1 class="m-title">
          Your work.
          <br />
          Your world.
          <br />
          <em>Yours to keep.</em>
        </h1>
        <p class="m-lede">
          An open workspace for your notes, projects, and saved knowledge. It starts on your device.
          It grows on your terms.
        </p>
        <div class="m-actions">
          <a class="m-button" href="/download">
            Try xNet <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
          </a>
          <a class="m-button secondary" href="/why">
            Explore the vision <span aria-hidden="true">→</span>
          </a>
        </div>
        <p class="m-note mt-5">
          Free, open-source software. Early, useful, and still taking shape.
        </p>
      </div>
      <MeshGarden />
    </section>
    <div class="home-facts">
      <div class="m-wrap">
        <span>Local first</span>
        <span>Yours to change</span>
        <span>Open by design</span>
        <a href="/commitments">Our commitments ↗</a>
      </div>
    </div>
    <section class="m-section" id="app">
      <div class="m-wrap">
        <div class="m-section-top">
          <div>
            <p class="m-eyebrow">01 / The workspace today</p>
            <h2 class="m-heading">
              A useful place
              <br />
              to <em>start.</em>
            </h2>
          </div>
          <p class="m-copy max-w-md">
            Write something down. Give a project some shape. Bring the things you care about into
            one place.
          </p>
        </div>
        <WorkspaceImage />
        <div class="m-grid-3 mt-12">
          <div class="m-step">
            <span class="m-note">01 — WRITE</span>
            <h3>Room for a thought.</h3>
            <p>
              Documents for notes, plans, and the ideas you’re still working out. Keep editing when
              you’re offline.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="m-step">
            <span class="m-note">02 — ORGANISE</span>
            <h3>Shape the moving parts.</h3>
            <p>
              Databases and canvases turn loose pieces into something you can work with, in the same
              workspace.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="m-step">
            <span class="m-note">03 — COLLECT · DESKTOP</span>
            <h3>A library of your own.</h3>
            <p>
              Save links and imported sources alongside your notes. Keep the context that made them
              worth saving.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="m-actions">
          <a class="m-text-link" href="/workspace">
            Meet the workspace <span aria-hidden="true">→</span>
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
    <section class="vision-band" id="open">
      <div class="m-wrap m-grid-2">
        <div>
          <p class="m-eyebrow">02 / The idea underneath</p>
          <h2 class="m-heading">
            Your data is the ground.
            <br />
            <em>Apps are the weather.</em>
          </h2>
          <a href="/why" class="m-text-link">
            Why we’re building xNet <span aria-hidden="true">→</span>
          </a>
        </div>
        <div class="m-copy">
          <p>
            You spend years gathering ideas, making things, and finding people worth listening to.
            That work should belong to you for longer than a service’s business model.
          </p>
          <p>
            We’re building toward a web where you keep the ground beneath your feet. Different tools
            can grow around the same data. A community can keep its history when a server closes.
            People can leave, return, and build something the original makers never imagined.
          </p>
          <p>
            It begins with a smaller, practical thing:{' '}
            <strong>a workspace whose master copy lives with you.</strong>
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
    <section class="m-section">
      <div class="m-wrap">
        <div class="m-section-top">
          <div>
            <p class="m-eyebrow">03 / A direction, not a finished promise</p>
            <h2 class="m-heading">
              Small beginnings.
              <br />
              <em>An open horizon.</em>
            </h2>
          </div>
          <a class="m-text-link" href="/roadmap">
            Follow the roadmap <span aria-hidden="true">→</span>
          </a>
        </div>
        <div class="m-grid-3">
          <article class="m-step">
            <span class="m-status now">Available now · Alpha</span>
            <h3>A workspace you can use.</h3>
            <p>
              Documents, databases, canvases, a desktop library, and the open foundations
              underneath. Start with the browser demo or desktop release.
            </p>
          </article>
          <article class="m-step">
            <span class="m-status">Being built</span>
            <h3>Tools that work with you.</h3>
            <p>
              More dependable daily use, easier sync and hosting, and AI that can do useful work
              with clear permission and a trail you can read.
            </p>
          </article>
          <article class="m-step">
            <span class="m-status">The longer view</span>
            <h3>A commons we can grow.</h3>
            <p>
              People sharing tools, knowledge, and spaces across an open network. Your identity and
              your work should travel with you.
            </p>
          </article>
        </div>
        <div class="m-banner mt-12">
          <p>
            <strong>About AI.</strong> Developer tools exist today. The easy, integrated experience
            we want is still being built. You don’t need an agent to use xNet.
          </p>
          <a class="m-text-link shrink-0" href="/agents">
            Where AI stands →
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
    <section class="m-section">
      <div class="m-wrap">
        <div class="m-section-top">
          <div>
            <p class="m-eyebrow">04 / Field notes from the open web</p>
            <h2 class="m-heading">
              The ideas we’re
              <br />
              <em>building with.</em>
            </h2>
          </div>
          <a href="/blog" class="m-text-link">
            Read all the essays <span aria-hidden="true">→</span>
          </a>
        </div>
        <div class="m-grid-3">
          {essays.map((essay) => (
            <a class="m-essay" href={`/blog/${essay.slug}`}>
              <BlogArt
                slug={essay.slug}
                class="m-essay-image"
                sizes="(max-width: 800px) 100vw, 33vw"
              />
              <p class="m-eyebrow mt-5">{essay.label}</p>
              <h3>{essay.title}</h3>
              <p>{essay.text}</p>
            </a>
          ))}
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
    <section class="m-section" id="developers">
      <div class="m-wrap">
        <div class="m-grid-2">
          <div>
            <p class="m-eyebrow">05 / For people who make things</p>
            <h2 class="m-heading mt-6">
              Small pieces.
              <br />
              <em>Room to build.</em>
            </h2>
          </div>
          <div class="m-copy">
            <p>
              Think of a box of building bricks. The pieces share a way to fit together, so you can
              take one creation apart and make another.
            </p>
            <p>
              xNet’s <strong>substrate</strong> is the shared data layer underneath the workspace.
              It gives builders reusable records, a common way to describe them, and rules for
              syncing and sharing. The app is one thing you can build from those parts.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <Substrate />
        <div class="m-actions">
          <a href="/build-with" class="m-button secondary">
            Build with xNet ↗
          </a>
          <a href="/blog/clutch-power" class="m-text-link">
            The idea behind the pieces →
          </a>
        </div>
        <p class="m-note mt-5">
          Open foundations, available in the alpha SDK. A broad ecosystem of interchangeable tools
          is the longer-term vision.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>
    <Closing />
  </main>
  <Footer />
</Base>
<style>
  .home-hero {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: 48px;
    align-items: center;
    padding-block: 76px 82px;
  }
  .home-hero .m-lede {
    max-width: 465px;
    font-size: 18px;
  }
  .home-hero .m-title {
    font-size: clamp(56px, 6.5vw, 88px);
  }
  .home-facts {
    border-block: 1px solid var(--rule);
  }
  .home-facts .m-wrap {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 20px;
    padding-block: 19px;
    font:
      10px ui-monospace,
      monospace;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.09em;
  }
  .vision-band {
    background: var(--wash);
    padding-block: 110px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule);
  }
  .vision-band .m-heading {
    margin-block: 30px 40px;
  }
  @media (max-width: 800px) {
    .home-hero {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      padding-block: 50px;
      gap: 35px;
    }
    .home-hero :global(.mesh-garden) {
      max-width: 470px;
      width: 100%;
      margin: auto;
    }
    .home-facts .m-wrap {
      flex-wrap: wrap;
      font-size: 9px;
    }
    .vision-band {
      padding-block: 64px;
    }
  }
</style>
